{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791029863,"nonce":"ZkbrlIBeRxo+1mYNc8KoaTD1pe4=","title":"SVG text shapes with system fonts, not the ones blinc_text loaded","message":"`rasterize::options_for` hands usvg a database built from\n`load_system_fonts()`. blinc_text keeps its own `FontRegistry`, with\nwhatever an app registered through `load_font_data` — bundled faces, the\nNoto subsets, anything fetched at runtime on web.\n\nThe two never meet. An SVG asking for a family the UI has loaded but the\nsystem has not falls back silently, so `\u003ctext\u003e` inside an icon can be\nshaped in a different typeface from the label beside it. On web and\nmobile, where `load_system_fonts()` finds little or nothing, that is the\nnormal case rather than an edge one.\n\nWants the two pointed at one database, or blinc_text's registered faces\npushed into usvg's. Either way the font a document names should resolve\nthe way it would for a text node.\n\nSplit out of b8860ee, which gave usvg a database at all and is fixed.\nThe ashui session offered to add a probe using a font only the UI has\nloaded, once this lands.","files":null}]}